# Google Custom Search API Configuration
# Required only for the separate Google Search integration, not Azure Bing webSearch.

# Google API Key - Get from Google Cloud Console
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Enable Custom Search API
# 3. Create credentials (API Key)
GOOGLE_CLOUD_API_KEY=

# Google Custom Search Engine ID
# 1. Go to https://programmablesearchengine.google.com/
# 2. Create a new search engine
# 3. Set to search the entire web
# 4. Copy the Search Engine ID
GOOGLE_CSE_ID=

# Optional: SerpAPI Key for the separate Google integration (not a Bing fallback)
# Get from https://serpapi.com/
# Paid service with free tier
SERPAPI_KEY=

# Azure Bing web search: HTTP POST /openai/v1/responses with store:false.
# Optional dedicated pair; if either is set, both are required. Do not mix pairs.
# AZURE_OPENAI_SEARCH_ENDPOINT=
# AZURE_OPENAI_SEARCH_API_KEY=
# Otherwise use this Microsoft pair if either is set (both required).
MICROSOFT_AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=
MICROSOFT_AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Otherwise use the generic pair (both required).
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Deployment precedence is independent: SEARCH, then MICROSOFT, then generic.
# Use an existing reasoning-enabled deployment with web_search_call.results.
# Tested model: gpt-5.2; this configuration does not create a deployment.
# AZURE_OPENAI_SEARCH_DEPLOYMENT=
MICROSOFT_AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=
AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=
# Default budgets: basic=1 tool call/low reasoning; advanced=2/medium;
# comprehensive=3/medium. No guarantee of equivalent Tavily search depth.
# max_results is a local cap up to 20, not a provider result-count guarantee.
# include_images:true, raw content and hard date filters are unsupported/rejected.
# No invented relevance score. Credits stay 0.1/query; Azure cost is tokens +
# Bing num_requests. Indexed/cached data, not live scraping; Bing compliance is separate.
# Review Bing terms/data handling; store:false does not guarantee Bing retention,
# residency or compliance parity with Azure model processing.
# API-server Azure secrets must be configured on Vercel, never NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
# No private .env edits or deployment are performed by this template migration.

# App URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
